**IMPORTANT**: Generate ONLY the `_app.tsx` file for Next.js. This is the app wrapper component.

# GOAL
Create the Next.js _app.tsx file that sets up the Convex provider for the entire application.

# CONTEXT
This wraps the entire Next.js app with ConvexProvider so all pages can use Convex queries.

# STACK
- Next.js 14
- Convex React client
- TypeScript

# ARTIFACTS
- `pages/_app.tsx`: App wrapper with Convex provider (implementation only, no tests)

# FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
- Import ConvexProvider and ConvexReactClient from 'convex/react'
- Import AppProps from 'next/app'
- Create ConvexReactClient instance with process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL
- Export default App component that wraps children with ConvexProvider
- Pass the convex client to ConvexProvider

# INTERFACE
```typescript
import { ConvexProvider, ConvexReactClient } from 'convex/react';
import type { AppProps } from 'next/app';

const convex = new ConvexReactClient(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL!);

export default function App({ Component, pageProps }: AppProps) {
  return (
    <ConvexProvider client={convex}>
      <Component {...pageProps} />
    </ConvexProvider>
  );
}
```

# VERIFICATION
✅ Creates ConvexReactClient with environment variable
✅ Wraps app with ConvexProvider
✅ Passes Component and pageProps correctly
